{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"readme-header-images","children":[{"type":"text","value":"README header images"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET /api/readme/<libraryId>.png"},{"type":"text","value":" renders the banner that goes at the top of a\nlibrary repo's README, replacing the hand-made PNGs previously committed to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"media/header_*.png"},{"type":"text","value":" in each repo. It uses the same takumi renderer, brand\nassets and per-category accent colors as the site's OG cards, so a branding\nchange ships to every README at once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Output is 1800×450 (4:1). At GitHub's ~896px README content width that renders\nat 2x and takes up ~224px of height, leaving the badges and intro above the\nfold."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<img\n  src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n  alt=\"TanStack Query\"\n  width=\"900\"\n/>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"light-and-dark","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Light and dark"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"?theme=dark"},{"type":"text","value":" renders the banner on the dark surface. Serve both through a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<picture>"},{"type":"text","value":" so GitHub picks the one matching the reader's theme — this is the\napproach GitHub documents in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.blog/developer-skills/github/how-to-make-your-images-in-markdown-on-github-adjust-for-dark-mode-and-light-mode/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to make your images in Markdown on GitHub adjust for dark mode and light mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<picture>\n  <source\n    media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\n    srcset=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png?theme=dark\"\n  />\n  <source\n    media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\n    srcset=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n  />\n  <img\n    src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n    alt=\"TanStack Query\"\n    width=\"900\"\n  />\n</picture>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The trailing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<img>"},{"type":"text","value":" is the fallback for renderers that ignore "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<picture>"},{"type":"text","value":"\n(npm, most editors), so it should stay the light variant."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same post describes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#gh-dark-mode-only"},{"type":"text","value":" URL-fragment trick. Prefer\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<picture>"},{"type":"text","value":": the fragment approach renders both images in any client that\ndoesn't special-case it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a package README inside a multi-framework repo (e.g.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/react-start/README.md"},{"type":"text","value":"), add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"?framework="},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<img\n  src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/start.png?framework=react\"\n  alt=\"TanStack React Start\"\n  width=\"900\"\n/>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The framework label is inserted after the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStack"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"react"},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack React Start"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Param"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"path splat"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library id ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"router"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":", …). Unknown id → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"404"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Must be one of the library's supported frameworks. Anything else → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"400"},{"type":"text","value":" listing the accepted values."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replaces the rendered name entirely. Clamped to 80 chars. Takes precedence over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"},{"type":"text","value":", which is then not applied."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subtitle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replaces the tagline. Clamped to 160 chars."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"light"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dark"},{"type":"text","value":". Anything else → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"400"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An invalid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"},{"type":"text","value":" is rejected rather than ignored, so a typo in a README\nshows up as a broken image during review instead of a banner naming the wrong\npackage."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"caching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caching"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The endpoint sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max-age=3600"},{"type":"text","value":" plus a 24h Cloudflare CDN TTL with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stale-while-revalidate"},{"type":"text","value":". GitHub additionally proxies README images through\ncamo, which caches on its own schedule — expect a banner change to take a while\nto appear on GitHub even after the endpoint updates. That is fine for branding\nassets; don't use this endpoint for anything time-sensitive."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"previewing-changes-locally","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Previewing changes locally"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm run readme:preview","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders every library's header in both themes — plus one per supported\nframework — to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".readme-preview/"},{"type":"text","value":", along with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index.html"},{"type":"text","value":" gallery that\ndisplays them at GitHub's 900px render width, each on its own theme surface.\nOpen "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".readme-preview/index.html"},{"type":"text","value":" to check that no long name or tagline\noverflows. Run this after touching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/server/og/readme-template.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts/og-preview.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" is the equivalent for the 1200×630 social cards.)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"implementation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implementation"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Role"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/api/readme/{$}[.]png.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route handler: param parsing, validation, cache headers"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/server/og/generate.server.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateReadmeHeaderResponse"},{"type":"text","value":" + the render path shared with OG"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/server/og/readme-template.tsx"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The 1800×450 layout"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/server/og/assets.server.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loads fonts and both raster brand emblems"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/server/og/colors.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category accents and surfaces per theme"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts/generate-brand-assets.mjs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generates the charcoal and cream 256px emblem rasters"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts/readme-header-preview.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Local render + gallery for reviewing layout changes"}]}]]}],"headings":[{"id":"readme-header-images","text":"README header images","level":1},{"id":"usage","text":"Usage","level":2},{"id":"light-and-dark","text":"Light and dark","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"caching","text":"Caching","level":2},{"id":"previewing-changes-locally","text":"Previewing changes locally","level":2},{"id":"implementation","text":"Implementation","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# README header images\n\n`GET /api/readme/<libraryId>.png` renders the banner that goes at the top of a\nlibrary repo's README, replacing the hand-made PNGs previously committed to\n`media/header_*.png` in each repo. It uses the same takumi renderer, brand\nassets and per-category accent colors as the site's OG cards, so a branding\nchange ships to every README at once.\n\nOutput is 1800×450 (4:1). At GitHub's ~896px README content width that renders\nat 2x and takes up ~224px of height, leaving the badges and intro above the\nfold.\n\n## Usage\n\n```html\n<img\n  src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n  alt=\"TanStack Query\"\n  width=\"900\"\n/>\n```\n\n### Light and dark\n\n`?theme=dark` renders the banner on the dark surface. Serve both through a\n`<picture>` so GitHub picks the one matching the reader's theme — this is the\napproach GitHub documents in\n[How to make your images in Markdown on GitHub adjust for dark mode and light mode](https://github.blog/developer-skills/github/how-to-make-your-images-in-markdown-on-github-adjust-for-dark-mode-and-light-mode/):\n\n```html\n<picture>\n  <source\n    media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\n    srcset=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png?theme=dark\"\n  />\n  <source\n    media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\n    srcset=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n  />\n  <img\n    src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n    alt=\"TanStack Query\"\n    width=\"900\"\n  />\n</picture>\n```\n\nThe trailing `<img>` is the fallback for renderers that ignore `<picture>`\n(npm, most editors), so it should stay the light variant.\n\nThe same post describes a `#gh-dark-mode-only` URL-fragment trick. Prefer\n`<picture>`: the fragment approach renders both images in any client that\ndoesn't special-case it.\n\nFor a package README inside a multi-framework repo (e.g.\n`packages/react-start/README.md`), add `?framework=`:\n\n```html\n<img\n  src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/start.png?framework=react\"\n  alt=\"TanStack React Start\"\n  width=\"900\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe framework label is inserted after the `TanStack` prefix:\n`start` + `react` → **TanStack React Start**.\n\n## Parameters\n\n| Param       | Required | Behavior                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| path splat  | yes      | Library id (`query`, `router`, `start`, …). Unknown id → `404`.                                                         |\n| `framework` | no       | Must be one of the library's supported frameworks. Anything else → `400` listing the accepted values.                   |\n| `title`     | no       | Replaces the rendered name entirely. Clamped to 80 chars. Takes precedence over `framework`, which is then not applied. |\n| `subtitle`  | no       | Replaces the tagline. Clamped to 160 chars.                                                                             |\n| `theme`     | no       | `light` (default) or `dark`. Anything else → `400`.                                                                     |\n\nAn invalid `framework` is rejected rather than ignored, so a typo in a README\nshows up as a broken image during review instead of a banner naming the wrong\npackage.\n\n## Caching\n\nThe endpoint sends `max-age=3600` plus a 24h Cloudflare CDN TTL with\n`stale-while-revalidate`. GitHub additionally proxies README images through\ncamo, which caches on its own schedule — expect a banner change to take a while\nto appear on GitHub even after the endpoint updates. That is fine for branding\nassets; don't use this endpoint for anything time-sensitive.\n\n## Previewing changes locally\n\n```sh\npnpm run readme:preview\n```\n\nRenders every library's header in both themes — plus one per supported\nframework — to `.readme-preview/`, along with an `index.html` gallery that\ndisplays them at GitHub's 900px render width, each on its own theme surface.\nOpen `.readme-preview/index.html` to check that no long name or tagline\noverflows. Run this after touching `src/server/og/readme-template.tsx`.\n\n(`scripts/og-preview.ts` is the equivalent for the 1200×630 social cards.)\n\n## Implementation\n\n| File                                 | Role                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/routes/api/readme/{$}[.]png.ts` | Route handler: param parsing, validation, cache headers         |\n| `src/server/og/generate.server.ts`   | `generateReadmeHeaderResponse` + the render path shared with OG |\n| `src/server/og/readme-template.tsx`  | The 1800×450 layout                                             |\n| `src/server/og/assets.server.ts`     | Loads fonts and both raster brand emblems                       |\n| `src/server/og/colors.ts`            | Category accents and surfaces per theme                         |\n| `scripts/generate-brand-assets.mjs`  | Generates the charcoal and cream 256px emblem rasters           |\n| `scripts/readme-header-preview.ts`   | Local render + gallery for reviewing layout changes             |\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# README header images\n\n`GET /api/readme/<libraryId>.png` renders the banner that goes at the top of a\nlibrary repo's README, replacing the hand-made PNGs previously committed to\n`media/header_*.png` in each repo. It uses the same takumi renderer, brand\nassets and per-category accent colors as the site's OG cards, so a branding\nchange ships to every README at once.\n\nOutput is 1800×450 (4:1). At GitHub's ~896px README content width that renders\nat 2x and takes up ~224px of height, leaving the badges and intro above the\nfold.\n\n## Usage\n\n```html\n<img\n  src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n  alt=\"TanStack Query\"\n  width=\"900\"\n/>\n```\n\n### Light and dark\n\n`?theme=dark` renders the banner on the dark surface. Serve both through a\n`<picture>` so GitHub picks the one matching the reader's theme — this is the\napproach GitHub documents in\n[How to make your images in Markdown on GitHub adjust for dark mode and light mode](https://github.blog/developer-skills/github/how-to-make-your-images-in-markdown-on-github-adjust-for-dark-mode-and-light-mode/):\n\n```html\n<picture>\n  <source\n    media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\n    srcset=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png?theme=dark\"\n  />\n  <source\n    media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\n    srcset=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n  />\n  <img\n    src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/query.png\"\n    alt=\"TanStack Query\"\n    width=\"900\"\n  />\n</picture>\n```\n\nThe trailing `<img>` is the fallback for renderers that ignore `<picture>`\n(npm, most editors), so it should stay the light variant.\n\nThe same post describes a `#gh-dark-mode-only` URL-fragment trick. Prefer\n`<picture>`: the fragment approach renders both images in any client that\ndoesn't special-case it.\n\nFor a package README inside a multi-framework repo (e.g.\n`packages/react-start/README.md`), add `?framework=`:\n\n```html\n<img\n  src=\"https://tanstack.com/api/readme/start.png?framework=react\"\n  alt=\"TanStack React Start\"\n  width=\"900\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe framework label is inserted after the `TanStack` prefix:\n`start` + `react` → **TanStack React Start**.\n\n## Parameters\n\n| Param       | Required | Behavior                                                                                                                |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| path splat  | yes      | Library id (`query`, `router`, `start`, …). Unknown id → `404`.                                                         |\n| `framework` | no       | Must be one of the library's supported frameworks. Anything else → `400` listing the accepted values.                   |\n| `title`     | no       | Replaces the rendered name entirely. Clamped to 80 chars. Takes precedence over `framework`, which is then not applied. |\n| `subtitle`  | no       | Replaces the tagline. Clamped to 160 chars.                                                                             |\n| `theme`     | no       | `light` (default) or `dark`. Anything else → `400`.                                                                     |\n\nAn invalid `framework` is rejected rather than ignored, so a typo in a README\nshows up as a broken image during review instead of a banner naming the wrong\npackage.\n\n## Caching\n\nThe endpoint sends `max-age=3600` plus a 24h Cloudflare CDN TTL with\n`stale-while-revalidate`. GitHub additionally proxies README images through\ncamo, which caches on its own schedule — expect a banner change to take a while\nto appear on GitHub even after the endpoint updates. That is fine for branding\nassets; don't use this endpoint for anything time-sensitive.\n\n## Previewing changes locally\n\n```sh\npnpm run readme:preview\n```\n\nRenders every library's header in both themes — plus one per supported\nframework — to `.readme-preview/`, along with an `index.html` gallery that\ndisplays them at GitHub's 900px render width, each on its own theme surface.\nOpen `.readme-preview/index.html` to check that no long name or tagline\noverflows. Run this after touching `src/server/og/readme-template.tsx`.\n\n(`scripts/og-preview.ts` is the equivalent for the 1200×630 social cards.)\n\n## Implementation\n\n| File                                 | Role                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/routes/api/readme/{$}[.]png.ts` | Route handler: param parsing, validation, cache headers         |\n| `src/server/og/generate.server.ts`   | `generateReadmeHeaderResponse` + the render path shared with OG |\n| `src/server/og/readme-template.tsx`  | The 1800×450 layout                                             |\n| `src/server/og/assets.server.ts`     | Loads fonts and both raster brand emblems                       |\n| `src/server/og/colors.ts`            | Category accents and surfaces per theme                         |\n| `scripts/generate-brand-assets.mjs`  | Generates the charcoal and cream 256px emblem rasters           |\n| `scripts/readme-header-preview.ts`   | Local render + gallery for reviewing layout changes             |\n"}
